### =====================================================================
### Lost & Found Hub - IntelliJ HTTP Client requests
### 1. Start the app   2. Choose the "dev" environment (top right of this file)
### 3. Run the requests from top to bottom (each login stores its token automatically)
### =====================================================================

### ---------- AUTH ----------

### Register user 1 (item owner / finder)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arun Kumar",
  "email": "arun@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}

### Register user 2 (claimant)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Priya Devi",
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

### Login user 1 -> saves {{userToken}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arun@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

> {% client.global.set("userToken", response.body.data.token); %}

### Login user 2 -> saves {{claimerToken}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd123"
}

> {% client.global.set("claimerToken", response.body.data.token); %}

### Login admin -> saves {{adminToken}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.data.token); %}

### Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arun@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPass1"
}

### ---------- USER ----------

### My profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Update my profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arun Kumar S",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}

### My posted items
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/items?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### My claims
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### ---------- ITEMS ----------

### Post a FOUND item with image -> saves {{itemId}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemName"

Black Leather Wallet
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

Wallet
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Black wallet with a student ID card inside
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

Main Library
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="eventDate"

2026-01-15
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemType"

FOUND
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="wallet.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample-images/wallet.png
--WebAppBoundary--

> {% client.global.set("itemId", response.body.data.id); client.global.set("imageUrl", response.body.data.imageUrl); %}

### Post a LOST item without image
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemName"

Red Umbrella
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

Accessories
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Red foldable umbrella lost near the canteen
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

Canteen
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="eventDate"

2026-01-20
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemType"

LOST
--WebAppBoundary--

### Upload without login (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemName"

No login
--WebAppBoundary--

### List all items (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc

### Search by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?keyword=wallet

### Filter by category + location + type + status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?category=Wallet&location=library&type=FOUND&status=OPEN

### Item by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}

### Download item image (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{imageUrl}}

### Update item (owner or admin) - old image is kept when no new image is sent
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemName"

Black Leather Wallet (updated)
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

Wallet
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Black wallet with a student ID card and a bus pass
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

Main Library
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="eventDate"

2026-01-15
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="itemType"

FOUND
--WebAppBoundary--

### ---------- CLAIMS ----------

### Claim own item (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": {{itemId}},
  "proofDescription": "This is my own item and I want to claim it"
}

### Submit a claim as user 2 -> saves {{claimId}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": {{itemId}},
  "proofDescription": "The ID card inside has my name Priya Devi and roll number 21CS045"
}

> {% client.global.set("claimId", response.body.data.id); %}

### Duplicate pending claim (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": {{itemId}},
  "proofDescription": "Trying to claim the same item again"
}

### My claims
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/my
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### Claim details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### Track claim status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claimId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### ---------- ADMIN ----------

### Normal user calling an admin API (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Dashboard statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All items
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/items?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All claims (optional ?status=PENDING|APPROVED|REJECTED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/claims?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Pending claims
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/claims/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Reject a claim (remarks required) - run this OR the approve request below for the same claim
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/claims/{{claimId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "REJECTED",
  "adminRemarks": "Roll number does not match the ID card"
}

### Approve a claim (other pending claims for the item are rejected automatically)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/claims/{{claimId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "APPROVED",
  "adminRemarks": "ID card details verified"
}

### Change item status manually (OPEN | CLAIMED | RETURNED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/items/{{itemId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CLAIMED"
}

### Mark item as RETURNED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/items/{{itemId}}/returned
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ---------- NOTIFICATIONS ----------

### My notifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### Unread count
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### Mark one notification as read (replace 1 with a real id)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/1/read
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### Mark all as read
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{claimerToken}}

### ---------- DELETE / LOGOUT ----------

### Delete an item (owner or admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Logout (token stops working afterwards)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
